# rdb_changes_since_last_save (server.dirty) is command-granular in PeaDB — one increment per
# write command — whereas Redis increments it per actual value change, so a SETBIT/BITFIELD
# that writes the same value adds 0. Matching this needs per-command dirty deltas.
# Tracked in compat/delta.md item 18.
SETBIT/BITFIELD only increase dirty when the value changed
